{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte 5 bindings for TanStack AI, providing reactive factory functions for the headless client using Svelte runes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a typed headless chat UI, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../ui/svelte","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte Chat UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-svelte\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createregisterwebmcptools-tools-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register executable client tools during Svelte component initialization. Svelte removes them when the component is destroyed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a complete setup and behavior guide, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/webmcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebMCP Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools,\n    type CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions,\n  } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n  import { searchProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\n  const tools = [searchProducts];\n  const options: CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<typeof tools> = {\n    onError(error) {\n      console.error(error);\n    },\n  };\n\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options);\n</script>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<TTools, TContext>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":". The factory owns the registration signal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" field is required when a tool declares a required runtime context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createpagewebmcptools-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createPageWebMCPTools(options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the WebMCP tools on the page as client tools. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" field starts empty and updates when the page adds or removes a tool. Read it in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get tools()"},{"type":"text","value":" getter on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createPageWebMCPTools } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools({\n    filter: (tool) => tool.origin === location.origin,\n  });\n</script>\n\n<p>{page.tools.length} page tools</p>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":" skips a tool when it returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":" gets a failed WebMCP read. For a complete guide, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/webmcp-page-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Page WebMCP Tools in Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createchathook-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bind "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" once at module scope. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat()"},{"type":"text","value":" to create the instance. Per-call overrides may set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialMessages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":". They must not change "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createChatHook, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n};\n\nconst { createChat } = createChatHook(chatOptions);\nconst chat = createChat({ threadId: \"support-1\" });","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat(chatOptions)"},{"type":"text","value":" from this package still works when you want to pass the full object at the call site. Rename the bound factory if both are in one file: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"const { createChat: createSupportChat } = createChatHook(chatOptions)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createchat-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Factory function for managing chat state in Svelte 5 with full type safety."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst updateUIDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"updateUI\",\n  description: \"Update the UI with a notification\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    message: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ success: z.boolean() }),\n});\n\n// In <script> block\nlet notification = \"\";\n\nconst updateUI = updateUIDef.client((input) => {\n  notification = input.message;\n  return { success: true };\n});\n\nconst tools = [updateUI];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\n// Fully typed messages!\ntype ChatMessages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n\nconst chat = createChat(chatOptions);\n// Access: chat.messages, chat.sendMessage, chat.isLoading, chat.error","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClientOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":" (minus internal state callbacks):"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"},{"type":"text","value":" - Connection adapter (required)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Array of client tool implementations (with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".client()"},{"type":"text","value":" method). In a component, read reactive state in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get tools()"},{"type":"text","value":" getter to change the tools after the chat is created."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialMessages?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Initial messages array"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId?"},{"type":"text","value":" - The only identity for this chat. Required when persistence is on. If omitted, minted after mount."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Arbitrary client-controlled JSON forwarded to the server in the AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunAgentInput.forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" field (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ provider: 'openai', model: 'gpt-5.5' }"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body?"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. Still works for backward compatibility; values are merged into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" on the wire"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Optional BYOK keyring from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineByok"},{"type":"text","value":". On each send the client prepares the resolved provider and stamps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" request headers. Keys never go in the body"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokProvider?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Optional function that returns the provider slug for this chat. If it returns a slug, only that key is prepared and sent. Otherwise the merged "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":", and per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" is used. Later sources win. If no slug resolves, the send throws instead of attaching every stored key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Typed client-local runtime context passed to client tool implementations. This value is not serialized to the server"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Enable live subscription mode (subscribes on creation)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResponse?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when response is received"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when stream chunk is received"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when response finishes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when error occurs"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptStateChange?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when interrupt state changes; context source is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" for restored state and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live"},{"type":"text","value":" for streamed or client-initiated updates"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCustomEvent?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback for custom stream events"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamProcessor?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Stream processing configuration"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Client tools are now automatically executed - no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" callback needed!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type {\n  UIMessage,\n  MultimodalContent,\n  ChatClientState,\n  ConnectionStatus,\n  SendMessageOptions,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\ninterface CreateChatReturn<TContext = unknown> {\n  readonly messages: UIMessage[];\n  sendMessage: (\n    content: string | MultimodalContent,\n    options?: SendMessageOptions,\n  ) => Promise<void>;\n  append: (message: ModelMessage | UIMessage) => Promise<void>;\n  addToolResult: (result: {\n    toolCallId: string;\n    tool: string;\n    output: any;\n    state?: \"output-available\" | \"output-error\";\n    errorText?: string;\n  }) => Promise<void>;\n  addToolApprovalResponse: (response: {\n    id: string;\n    approved: boolean;\n  }) => Promise<void>;\n  reload: () => Promise<void>;\n  stop: () => void;\n  readonly isLoading: boolean;\n  readonly error: Error | undefined;\n  readonly status: ChatClientState;\n  readonly isSubscribed: boolean;\n  readonly connectionStatus: ConnectionStatus;\n  readonly sessionGenerating: boolean;\n  readonly isHydrating: boolean;\n  setMessages: (messages: UIMessage[]) => void;\n  clear: () => void;\n  /** @deprecated Use `updateForwardedProps` instead. */\n  updateBody: (body: Record<string, any>) => void;\n  updateForwardedProps: (forwardedProps: Record<string, any>) => void;\n  updateContext: (context: TContext) => void;\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key differences from React/Vue:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":" naming"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- factory functions, not hooks. Call outside of any lifecycle."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive getters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- state properties ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSubscribed"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connectionStatus"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionGenerating"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isHydrating"},{"type":"text","value":") are Svelte 5 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$state"},{"type":"text","value":" via getters. Access directly (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.messages"},{"type":"text","value":", not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.messages.value"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No automatic cleanup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- unlike React/Vue/Solid, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat"},{"type":"text","value":" does not auto-dispose. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" manually when the component unmounts (e.g., in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDestroy"},{"type":"text","value":" or an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$effect"},{"type":"text","value":" return)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateForwardedProps()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- update AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" dynamically (e.g., for model selection). In Vue, changes to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" option are synced via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watch"},{"type":"text","value":"; in Svelte, call this method explicitly. The legacy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateBody()"},{"type":"text","value":" is still available but deprecated."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".svelte.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" files"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- source files use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".svelte.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" extension for Svelte 5 rune support."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createbyok-client","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createByok(client)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subscribe to a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ByokClient"},{"type":"text","value":" snapshot in Svelte 5. Call it during component init."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nconst byokState = createByok(byok);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the object. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokState.snapshot"},{"type":"text","value":" is a reactive getter ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"locked"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":"). Destructuring "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshot"},{"type":"text","value":" freezes the first value. Read it in markup or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$derived"},{"type":"text","value":". Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.update(provider, value)"},{"type":"text","value":" from your own UI to save a key. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"connection-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connection Adapters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":" for convenience:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  fetchHttpStream,\n  fetchJson,\n  stream,\n  type ConnectionAdapter,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-basic-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Basic Chat"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  let input = $state(\"\");\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (e: Event) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\n      chat.sendMessage(input);\n      input = \"\";\n    }\n  };\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  <div>\n    {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n      <div>\n        <strong>{message.role}:</strong>\n        {#each message.parts as part, idx}\n          {#if part.type === \"thinking\"}\n            <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 italic\">\n              Thinking: {part.content}\n            </div>\n          {:else if part.type === \"text\"}\n            <span>{part.content}</span>\n          {/if}\n        {/each}\n      </div>\n    {/each}\n  </div>\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n    <button type=\"submit\" disabled={chat.isLoading}>Send</button>\n  </form>\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Tool Approval"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    {#each message.parts as part}\n      {#if part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.state === \"approval-requested\" && part.approval}\n        <div>\n          <p>Approve: {part.name}</p>\n          <button\n            onclick={() =>\n              chat.addToolApprovalResponse({\n                id: part.approval.id,\n                approved: true,\n              })}\n          >\n            Approve\n          </button>\n          <button\n            onclick={() =>\n              chat.addToolApprovalResponse({\n                id: part.approval.id,\n                approved: false,\n              })}\n          >\n            Deny\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      {/if}\n    {/each}\n  {/each}\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-client-tools-with-type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Client Tools with Type Safety"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n  import {\n    createChatClientOptions,\n    type InferChatMessages,\n  } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n  import { updateUIDef, saveToStorageDef } from \"./tool-definitions\";\n\n  let notification = $state(null);\n\n  // Create client implementations\n  const updateUI = updateUIDef.client((input) => {\n    // input is fully typed!\n    notification = { message: input.message, type: input.type };\n    return { success: true };\n  });\n\n  const saveToStorage = saveToStorageDef.client((input) => {\n    localStorage.setItem(input.key, input.value);\n    return { saved: true };\n  });\n\n  // Create typed tools array (no 'as const' needed!)\n  const tools = [updateUI, saveToStorage];\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    tools, // Automatic execution, full type safety\n  });\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    {#each message.parts as part}\n      {#if part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.name === \"updateUI\"}\n        <div>Tool executed: {part.name}</div>\n      {/if}\n    {/each}\n  {/each}\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"generation-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Factory functions for one-shot generation tasks (images, speech, transcription, summarization, video). All share the same pattern: provide a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher"},{"type":"text","value":", call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":", and read reactive state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creategeneration-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGeneration(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Base factory for custom generation types. All specialized functions below are built on this."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createGeneration, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\nconst gen = createGeneration({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/generate/custom\"),\n});\n\n// gen.generate({ prompt: 'Hello' })\n// gen.result, gen.isLoading, gen.error, gen.status","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onProgress?"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateBody"},{"type":"text","value":" -- all state properties are reactive getters."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creategenerateimage-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateImage(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image generation factory. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":", result is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerationResult"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creategeneratespeech-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateSpeech(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-speech factory. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SpeechGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":", result is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TTSResult"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createtranscription-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTranscription(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio transcription factory. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TranscriptionGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":", result is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TranscriptionResult"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createsummarize-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSummarize(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text summarization factory. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SummarizeGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":", result is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SummarizationResult"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creategeneratevideo-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateVideo(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video generation factory with job polling. Returns additional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jobId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"videoStatus"},{"type":"text","value":" reactive getters. Accepts extra "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onJobCreated?"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStatusUpdate?"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No generation function includes automatic cleanup. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" manually when done."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createchatclientoptions-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatClientOptions(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper to create typed chat options (re-exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { tool1, tool2 } from \"./tools\";\n\n// Create typed tools array (no 'as const' needed!)\nconst tools = [tool1, tool2];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\ntype Messages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIMessage<TTools>"},{"type":"text","value":" - Message type with tool type parameter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MessagePart<TTools>"},{"type":"text","value":" - Message part with tool type parameter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextPart"},{"type":"text","value":" - Text content part"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" - Thinking content part"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCallPart<TTools>"},{"type":"text","value":" - Tool call part (discriminated union)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolResultPart"},{"type":"text","value":" - Tool result part"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClientOptions<TTools, TContext>"},{"type":"text","value":" - Chat client options with typed client runtime context"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ConnectionAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" - Connection adapter interface"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InferChatMessages<T>"},{"type":"text","value":" - Extract message type from options"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatRequestBody"},{"type":"text","value":" - Request body type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationClientState"},{"type":"text","value":" - Generation lifecycle state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":" - Image generation input type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SpeechGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":" - Speech generation input type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TranscriptionGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":" - Transcription input type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SummarizeGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":" - Summarization input type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":" - Video generation input type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoGenerateResult"},{"type":"text","value":" - Video generation result type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoStatusInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" - Video job status info"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" - Create isomorphic tool definition"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolDefinitionInstance"},{"type":"text","value":" - Tool definition type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ClientTool"},{"type":"text","value":" - Client tool type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ServerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" - Server tool type"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn the basics"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about the isomorphic tool system"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/client-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about client-side tools"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"createregisterwebmcptools-tools-options","text":"createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options?)","level":2},{"id":"createpagewebmcptools-options","text":"createPageWebMCPTools(options?)","level":2},{"id":"createchathook-options","text":"createChatHook(options)","level":2},{"id":"createchat-options","text":"createChat(options)","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"createbyok-client","text":"createByok(client)","level":2},{"id":"connection-adapters","text":"Connection Adapters","level":2},{"id":"example-basic-chat","text":"Example: Basic Chat","level":2},{"id":"example-tool-approval","text":"Example: Tool Approval","level":2},{"id":"example-client-tools-with-type-safety","text":"Example: Client Tools with Type Safety","level":2},{"id":"generation-functions","text":"Generation Functions","level":2},{"id":"creategeneration-options","text":"createGeneration(options)","level":3},{"id":"creategenerateimage-options","text":"createGenerateImage(options)","level":3},{"id":"creategeneratespeech-options","text":"createGenerateSpeech(options)","level":3},{"id":"createtranscription-options","text":"createTranscription(options)","level":3},{"id":"createsummarize-options","text":"createSummarize(options)","level":3},{"id":"creategeneratevideo-options","text":"createGenerateVideo(options)","level":3},{"id":"createchatclientoptions-options","text":"createChatClientOptions(options)","level":2},{"id":"types","text":"Types","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["svelte"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSvelte 5 bindings for TanStack AI, providing reactive factory functions for the headless client using Svelte runes.\n\nFor a typed headless chat UI, see [Svelte Chat UI](../ui/svelte).\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-svelte\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## `createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options?)`\n\nRegister executable client tools during Svelte component initialization. Svelte removes them when the component is destroyed.\n\nFor a complete setup and behavior guide, see [WebMCP Tools](../tools/webmcp).\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools,\n    type CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions,\n  } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n  import { searchProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\n  const tools = [searchProducts];\n  const options: CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<typeof tools> = {\n    onError(error) {\n      console.error(error);\n    },\n  };\n\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options);\n</script>\n```\n\n`CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<TTools, TContext>` contains `toolOptions`, `context`, and `onError`. The factory owns the registration signal.\n\nThe `context` field is required when a tool declares a required runtime context.\n\n## `createPageWebMCPTools(options?)`\n\nRead the WebMCP tools on the page as client tools. The `tools` field starts empty and updates when the page adds or removes a tool. Read it in a `get tools()` getter on `createChat`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createPageWebMCPTools } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools({\n    filter: (tool) => tool.origin === location.origin,\n  });\n</script>\n\n<p>{page.tools.length} page tools</p>\n```\n\n`filter` skips a tool when it returns `false`. `onError` gets a failed WebMCP read. For a complete guide, see [Page WebMCP Tools in Chat](../tools/webmcp-page-tools).\n\n## `createChatHook(options)`\n\nBind `chatOptions` once at module scope. Call `createChat()` to create the instance. Per-call overrides may set `threadId`, `initialMessages`, `live`, and `forwardedProps`. They must not change `tools`, `interrupts`, or `outputSchema`.\n\n```ts\nimport { createChatHook, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n};\n\nconst { createChat } = createChatHook(chatOptions);\nconst chat = createChat({ threadId: \"support-1\" });\n```\n\n`createChat(chatOptions)` from this package still works when you want to pass the full object at the call site. Rename the bound factory if both are in one file: `const { createChat: createSupportChat } = createChatHook(chatOptions)`.\n\n## `createChat(options)`\n\nFactory function for managing chat state in Svelte 5 with full type safety.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst updateUIDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"updateUI\",\n  description: \"Update the UI with a notification\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    message: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ success: z.boolean() }),\n});\n\n// In <script> block\nlet notification = \"\";\n\nconst updateUI = updateUIDef.client((input) => {\n  notification = input.message;\n  return { success: true };\n});\n\nconst tools = [updateUI];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\n// Fully typed messages!\ntype ChatMessages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n\nconst chat = createChat(chatOptions);\n// Access: chat.messages, chat.sendMessage, chat.isLoading, chat.error\n```\n\n### Options\n\nExtends `ChatClientOptions` from `@tanstack/ai-client` (minus internal state callbacks):\n\n- `connection` - Connection adapter (required)\n- `tools?` - Array of client tool implementations (with `.client()` method). In a component, read reactive state in a `get tools()` getter to change the tools after the chat is created.\n- `initialMessages?` - Initial messages array\n- `threadId?` - The only identity for this chat. Required when persistence is on. If omitted, minted after mount.\n- `forwardedProps?` - Arbitrary client-controlled JSON forwarded to the server in the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps` field (e.g., `{ provider: 'openai', model: 'gpt-5.5' }`)\n- `body?` - **Deprecated.** Use `forwardedProps` instead. Still works for backward compatibility; values are merged into `forwardedProps` on the wire\n- `byok?` - Optional BYOK keyring from `defineByok`. On each send the client prepares the resolved provider and stamps `x-byok-*` request headers. Keys never go in the body\n- `byokProvider?` - Optional function that returns the provider slug for this chat. If it returns a slug, only that key is prepared and sent. Otherwise the merged `provider` from `forwardedProps`, `body`, and per-call `sendMessage` `body` is used. Later sources win. If no slug resolves, the send throws instead of attaching every stored key\n- `context?` - Typed client-local runtime context passed to client tool implementations. This value is not serialized to the server\n- `live?` - Enable live subscription mode (subscribes on creation)\n- `onResponse?` - Callback when response is received\n- `onChunk?` - Callback when stream chunk is received\n- `onFinish?` - Callback when response finishes\n- `onError?` - Callback when error occurs\n- `onInterruptStateChange?` - Callback when interrupt state changes; context source is `hydrate` for restored state and `live` for streamed or client-initiated updates\n- `onCustomEvent?` - Callback for custom stream events\n- `streamProcessor?` - Stream processing configuration\n\n**Note:** Client tools are now automatically executed - no `onToolCall` callback needed!\n\n### Returns\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  UIMessage,\n  MultimodalContent,\n  ChatClientState,\n  ConnectionStatus,\n  SendMessageOptions,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\ninterface CreateChatReturn<TContext = unknown> {\n  readonly messages: UIMessage[];\n  sendMessage: (\n    content: string | MultimodalContent,\n    options?: SendMessageOptions,\n  ) => Promise<void>;\n  append: (message: ModelMessage | UIMessage) => Promise<void>;\n  addToolResult: (result: {\n    toolCallId: string;\n    tool: string;\n    output: any;\n    state?: \"output-available\" | \"output-error\";\n    errorText?: string;\n  }) => Promise<void>;\n  addToolApprovalResponse: (response: {\n    id: string;\n    approved: boolean;\n  }) => Promise<void>;\n  reload: () => Promise<void>;\n  stop: () => void;\n  readonly isLoading: boolean;\n  readonly error: Error | undefined;\n  readonly status: ChatClientState;\n  readonly isSubscribed: boolean;\n  readonly connectionStatus: ConnectionStatus;\n  readonly sessionGenerating: boolean;\n  readonly isHydrating: boolean;\n  setMessages: (messages: UIMessage[]) => void;\n  clear: () => void;\n  /** @deprecated Use `updateForwardedProps` instead. */\n  updateBody: (body: Record<string, any>) => void;\n  updateForwardedProps: (forwardedProps: Record<string, any>) => void;\n  updateContext: (context: TContext) => void;\n}\n```\n\n**Key differences from React/Vue:**\n\n- **`create*` naming** -- factory functions, not hooks. Call outside of any lifecycle.\n- **Reactive getters** -- state properties (`messages`, `isLoading`, `error`, `status`, `isSubscribed`, `connectionStatus`, `sessionGenerating`, `isHydrating`) are Svelte 5 `$state` via getters. Access directly (e.g., `chat.messages`, not `chat.messages.value`).\n- **No automatic cleanup** -- unlike React/Vue/Solid, `createChat` does not auto-dispose. Call `chat.stop()` manually when the component unmounts (e.g., in `onDestroy` or an `$effect` return).\n- **`updateForwardedProps()`** -- update AG-UI `forwardedProps` dynamically (e.g., for model selection). In Vue, changes to the `forwardedProps` option are synced via `watch`; in Svelte, call this method explicitly. The legacy `updateBody()` is still available but deprecated.\n- **`.svelte.ts` files** -- source files use the `.svelte.ts` extension for Svelte 5 rune support.\n\n## `createByok(client)`\n\nSubscribe to a `ByokClient` snapshot in Svelte 5. Call it during component init.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nconst byokState = createByok(byok);\n```\n\nKeep the object. `byokState.snapshot` is a reactive getter (`status`, `locked`, `prompt`). Destructuring `snapshot` freezes the first value. Read it in markup or `$derived`. Call `byok.update(provider, value)` from your own UI to save a key. See [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## Connection Adapters\n\nRe-exported from `@tanstack/ai-client` for convenience:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  fetchHttpStream,\n  fetchJson,\n  stream,\n  type ConnectionAdapter,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n```\n\n## Example: Basic Chat\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  let input = $state(\"\");\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (e: Event) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\n      chat.sendMessage(input);\n      input = \"\";\n    }\n  };\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  <div>\n    {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n      <div>\n        <strong>{message.role}:</strong>\n        {#each message.parts as part, idx}\n          {#if part.type === \"thinking\"}\n            <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 italic\">\n              Thinking: {part.content}\n            </div>\n          {:else if part.type === \"text\"}\n            <span>{part.content}</span>\n          {/if}\n        {/each}\n      </div>\n    {/each}\n  </div>\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n    <button type=\"submit\" disabled={chat.isLoading}>Send</button>\n  </form>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Example: Tool Approval\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    {#each message.parts as part}\n      {#if part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.state === \"approval-requested\" && part.approval}\n        <div>\n          <p>Approve: {part.name}</p>\n          <button\n            onclick={() =>\n              chat.addToolApprovalResponse({\n                id: part.approval.id,\n                approved: true,\n              })}\n          >\n            Approve\n          </button>\n          <button\n            onclick={() =>\n              chat.addToolApprovalResponse({\n                id: part.approval.id,\n                approved: false,\n              })}\n          >\n            Deny\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      {/if}\n    {/each}\n  {/each}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Example: Client Tools with Type Safety\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n  import {\n    createChatClientOptions,\n    type InferChatMessages,\n  } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n  import { updateUIDef, saveToStorageDef } from \"./tool-definitions\";\n\n  let notification = $state(null);\n\n  // Create client implementations\n  const updateUI = updateUIDef.client((input) => {\n    // input is fully typed!\n    notification = { message: input.message, type: input.type };\n    return { success: true };\n  });\n\n  const saveToStorage = saveToStorageDef.client((input) => {\n    localStorage.setItem(input.key, input.value);\n    return { saved: true };\n  });\n\n  // Create typed tools array (no 'as const' needed!)\n  const tools = [updateUI, saveToStorage];\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    tools, // Automatic execution, full type safety\n  });\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    {#each message.parts as part}\n      {#if part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.name === \"updateUI\"}\n        <div>Tool executed: {part.name}</div>\n      {/if}\n    {/each}\n  {/each}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Generation Functions\n\nFactory functions for one-shot generation tasks (images, speech, transcription, summarization, video). All share the same pattern: provide a `connection` or `fetcher`, call `generate()`, and read reactive state.\n\n### `createGeneration(options)`\n\nBase factory for custom generation types. All specialized functions below are built on this.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createGeneration, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\nconst gen = createGeneration({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/generate/custom\"),\n});\n\n// gen.generate({ prompt: 'Hello' })\n// gen.result, gen.isLoading, gen.error, gen.status\n```\n\n**Options:** `connection?`, `fetcher?`, `threadId?`, `body?`, `onResult?`, `onError?`, `onProgress?`, `onChunk?`\n\n**Returns:** `generate`, `result`, `isLoading`, `error`, `status`, `stop`, `reset`, `runId`, `updateBody` -- all state properties are reactive getters.\n\n### `createGenerateImage(options)`\n\nImage generation factory. `generate()` accepts `ImageGenerateInput`, result is `ImageGenerationResult`.\n\n### `createGenerateSpeech(options)`\n\nText-to-speech factory. `generate()` accepts `SpeechGenerateInput`, result is `TTSResult`.\n\n### `createTranscription(options)`\n\nAudio transcription factory. `generate()` accepts `TranscriptionGenerateInput`, result is `TranscriptionResult`.\n\n### `createSummarize(options)`\n\nText summarization factory. `generate()` accepts `SummarizeGenerateInput`, result is `SummarizationResult`.\n\n### `createGenerateVideo(options)`\n\nVideo generation factory with job polling. Returns additional `jobId` and `videoStatus` reactive getters. Accepts extra `onJobCreated?` and `onStatusUpdate?` callbacks.\n\nNo generation function includes automatic cleanup. Call `.stop()` manually when done.\n\n## `createChatClientOptions(options)`\n\nHelper to create typed chat options (re-exported from `@tanstack/ai-client`).\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { tool1, tool2 } from \"./tools\";\n\n// Create typed tools array (no 'as const' needed!)\nconst tools = [tool1, tool2];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\ntype Messages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n```\n\n## Types\n\nRe-exported from `@tanstack/ai-client`:\n\n- `UIMessage<TTools>` - Message type with tool type parameter\n- `MessagePart<TTools>` - Message part with tool type parameter\n- `TextPart` - Text content part\n- `ThinkingPart` - Thinking content part\n- `ToolCallPart<TTools>` - Tool call part (discriminated union)\n- `ToolResultPart` - Tool result part\n- `ChatClientOptions<TTools, TContext>` - Chat client options with typed client runtime context\n- `ConnectionAdapter` - Connection adapter interface\n- `InferChatMessages<T>` - Extract message type from options\n- `ChatRequestBody` - Request body type\n- `GenerationClientState` - Generation lifecycle state\n- `ImageGenerateInput` - Image generation input type\n- `SpeechGenerateInput` - Speech generation input type\n- `TranscriptionGenerateInput` - Transcription input type\n- `SummarizeGenerateInput` - Summarization input type\n- `VideoGenerateInput` - Video generation input type\n- `VideoGenerateResult` - Video generation result type\n- `VideoStatusInfo` - Video job status info\n\nRe-exported from `@tanstack/ai`:\n\n- `toolDefinition()` - Create isomorphic tool definition\n- `ToolDefinitionInstance` - Tool definition type\n- `ClientTool` - Client tool type\n- `ServerTool` - Server tool type\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n- [Client Tools](../tools/client-tools) - Learn about client-side tools\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\"\nid: ai-svelte\norder: 6\ndescription: \"API reference for @tanstack/ai-svelte — Svelte 5 reactive factory functions for streaming chat built on runes.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\"\n  - svelte\n  - svelte 5\n  - createChat\n  - runes\n  - api reference\n---\n\nSvelte 5 bindings for TanStack AI, providing reactive factory functions for the headless client using Svelte runes.\n\nFor a typed headless chat UI, see [Svelte Chat UI](../ui/svelte).\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-svelte\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## `createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options?)`\n\nRegister executable client tools during Svelte component initialization. Svelte removes them when the component is destroyed.\n\nFor a complete setup and behavior guide, see [WebMCP Tools](../tools/webmcp).\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools,\n    type CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions,\n  } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n  import { searchProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\n  const tools = [searchProducts];\n  const options: CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<typeof tools> = {\n    onError(error) {\n      console.error(error);\n    },\n  };\n\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(tools, options);\n</script>\n```\n\n`CreateRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<TTools, TContext>` contains `toolOptions`, `context`, and `onError`. The factory owns the registration signal.\n\nThe `context` field is required when a tool declares a required runtime context.\n\n## `createPageWebMCPTools(options?)`\n\nRead the WebMCP tools on the page as client tools. The `tools` field starts empty and updates when the page adds or removes a tool. Read it in a `get tools()` getter on `createChat`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createPageWebMCPTools } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools({\n    filter: (tool) => tool.origin === location.origin,\n  });\n</script>\n\n<p>{page.tools.length} page tools</p>\n```\n\n`filter` skips a tool when it returns `false`. `onError` gets a failed WebMCP read. For a complete guide, see [Page WebMCP Tools in Chat](../tools/webmcp-page-tools).\n\n## `createChatHook(options)`\n\nBind `chatOptions` once at module scope. Call `createChat()` to create the instance. Per-call overrides may set `threadId`, `initialMessages`, `live`, and `forwardedProps`. They must not change `tools`, `interrupts`, or `outputSchema`.\n\n```ts\nimport { createChatHook, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n};\n\nconst { createChat } = createChatHook(chatOptions);\nconst chat = createChat({ threadId: \"support-1\" });\n```\n\n`createChat(chatOptions)` from this package still works when you want to pass the full object at the call site. Rename the bound factory if both are in one file: `const { createChat: createSupportChat } = createChatHook(chatOptions)`.\n\n## `createChat(options)`\n\nFactory function for managing chat state in Svelte 5 with full type safety.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst updateUIDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"updateUI\",\n  description: \"Update the UI with a notification\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    message: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ success: z.boolean() }),\n});\n\n// In <script> block\nlet notification = \"\";\n\nconst updateUI = updateUIDef.client((input) => {\n  notification = input.message;\n  return { success: true };\n});\n\nconst tools = [updateUI];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\n// Fully typed messages!\ntype ChatMessages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n\nconst chat = createChat(chatOptions);\n// Access: chat.messages, chat.sendMessage, chat.isLoading, chat.error\n```\n\n### Options\n\nExtends `ChatClientOptions` from `@tanstack/ai-client` (minus internal state callbacks):\n\n- `connection` - Connection adapter (required)\n- `tools?` - Array of client tool implementations (with `.client()` method). In a component, read reactive state in a `get tools()` getter to change the tools after the chat is created.\n- `initialMessages?` - Initial messages array\n- `threadId?` - The only identity for this chat. Required when persistence is on. If omitted, minted after mount.\n- `forwardedProps?` - Arbitrary client-controlled JSON forwarded to the server in the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps` field (e.g., `{ provider: 'openai', model: 'gpt-5.5' }`)\n- `body?` - **Deprecated.** Use `forwardedProps` instead. Still works for backward compatibility; values are merged into `forwardedProps` on the wire\n- `byok?` - Optional BYOK keyring from `defineByok`. On each send the client prepares the resolved provider and stamps `x-byok-*` request headers. Keys never go in the body\n- `byokProvider?` - Optional function that returns the provider slug for this chat. If it returns a slug, only that key is prepared and sent. Otherwise the merged `provider` from `forwardedProps`, `body`, and per-call `sendMessage` `body` is used. Later sources win. If no slug resolves, the send throws instead of attaching every stored key\n- `context?` - Typed client-local runtime context passed to client tool implementations. This value is not serialized to the server\n- `live?` - Enable live subscription mode (subscribes on creation)\n- `onResponse?` - Callback when response is received\n- `onChunk?` - Callback when stream chunk is received\n- `onFinish?` - Callback when response finishes\n- `onError?` - Callback when error occurs\n- `onInterruptStateChange?` - Callback when interrupt state changes; context source is `hydrate` for restored state and `live` for streamed or client-initiated updates\n- `onCustomEvent?` - Callback for custom stream events\n- `streamProcessor?` - Stream processing configuration\n\n**Note:** Client tools are now automatically executed - no `onToolCall` callback needed!\n\n### Returns\n\n```typescript\nimport type {\n  UIMessage,\n  MultimodalContent,\n  ChatClientState,\n  ConnectionStatus,\n  SendMessageOptions,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\ninterface CreateChatReturn<TContext = unknown> {\n  readonly messages: UIMessage[];\n  sendMessage: (\n    content: string | MultimodalContent,\n    options?: SendMessageOptions,\n  ) => Promise<void>;\n  append: (message: ModelMessage | UIMessage) => Promise<void>;\n  addToolResult: (result: {\n    toolCallId: string;\n    tool: string;\n    output: any;\n    state?: \"output-available\" | \"output-error\";\n    errorText?: string;\n  }) => Promise<void>;\n  addToolApprovalResponse: (response: {\n    id: string;\n    approved: boolean;\n  }) => Promise<void>;\n  reload: () => Promise<void>;\n  stop: () => void;\n  readonly isLoading: boolean;\n  readonly error: Error | undefined;\n  readonly status: ChatClientState;\n  readonly isSubscribed: boolean;\n  readonly connectionStatus: ConnectionStatus;\n  readonly sessionGenerating: boolean;\n  readonly isHydrating: boolean;\n  setMessages: (messages: UIMessage[]) => void;\n  clear: () => void;\n  /** @deprecated Use `updateForwardedProps` instead. */\n  updateBody: (body: Record<string, any>) => void;\n  updateForwardedProps: (forwardedProps: Record<string, any>) => void;\n  updateContext: (context: TContext) => void;\n}\n```\n\n**Key differences from React/Vue:**\n\n- **`create*` naming** -- factory functions, not hooks. Call outside of any lifecycle.\n- **Reactive getters** -- state properties (`messages`, `isLoading`, `error`, `status`, `isSubscribed`, `connectionStatus`, `sessionGenerating`, `isHydrating`) are Svelte 5 `$state` via getters. Access directly (e.g., `chat.messages`, not `chat.messages.value`).\n- **No automatic cleanup** -- unlike React/Vue/Solid, `createChat` does not auto-dispose. Call `chat.stop()` manually when the component unmounts (e.g., in `onDestroy` or an `$effect` return).\n- **`updateForwardedProps()`** -- update AG-UI `forwardedProps` dynamically (e.g., for model selection). In Vue, changes to the `forwardedProps` option are synced via `watch`; in Svelte, call this method explicitly. The legacy `updateBody()` is still available but deprecated.\n- **`.svelte.ts` files** -- source files use the `.svelte.ts` extension for Svelte 5 rune support.\n\n## `createByok(client)`\n\nSubscribe to a `ByokClient` snapshot in Svelte 5. Call it during component init.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nconst byokState = createByok(byok);\n```\n\nKeep the object. `byokState.snapshot` is a reactive getter (`status`, `locked`, `prompt`). Destructuring `snapshot` freezes the first value. Read it in markup or `$derived`. Call `byok.update(provider, value)` from your own UI to save a key. See [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## Connection Adapters\n\nRe-exported from `@tanstack/ai-client` for convenience:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  fetchHttpStream,\n  fetchJson,\n  stream,\n  type ConnectionAdapter,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n```\n\n## Example: Basic Chat\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  let input = $state(\"\");\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (e: Event) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\n      chat.sendMessage(input);\n      input = \"\";\n    }\n  };\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  <div>\n    {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n      <div>\n        <strong>{message.role}:</strong>\n        {#each message.parts as part, idx}\n          {#if part.type === \"thinking\"}\n            <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 italic\">\n              Thinking: {part.content}\n            </div>\n          {:else if part.type === \"text\"}\n            <span>{part.content}</span>\n          {/if}\n        {/each}\n      </div>\n    {/each}\n  </div>\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n    <button type=\"submit\" disabled={chat.isLoading}>Send</button>\n  </form>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Example: Tool Approval\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    {#each message.parts as part}\n      {#if part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.state === \"approval-requested\" && part.approval}\n        <div>\n          <p>Approve: {part.name}</p>\n          <button\n            onclick={() =>\n              chat.addToolApprovalResponse({\n                id: part.approval.id,\n                approved: true,\n              })}\n          >\n            Approve\n          </button>\n          <button\n            onclick={() =>\n              chat.addToolApprovalResponse({\n                id: part.approval.id,\n                approved: false,\n              })}\n          >\n            Deny\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      {/if}\n    {/each}\n  {/each}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Example: Client Tools with Type Safety\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n  import {\n    createChatClientOptions,\n    type InferChatMessages,\n  } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n  import { updateUIDef, saveToStorageDef } from \"./tool-definitions\";\n\n  let notification = $state(null);\n\n  // Create client implementations\n  const updateUI = updateUIDef.client((input) => {\n    // input is fully typed!\n    notification = { message: input.message, type: input.type };\n    return { success: true };\n  });\n\n  const saveToStorage = saveToStorageDef.client((input) => {\n    localStorage.setItem(input.key, input.value);\n    return { saved: true };\n  });\n\n  // Create typed tools array (no 'as const' needed!)\n  const tools = [updateUI, saveToStorage];\n\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    tools, // Automatic execution, full type safety\n  });\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    {#each message.parts as part}\n      {#if part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.name === \"updateUI\"}\n        <div>Tool executed: {part.name}</div>\n      {/if}\n    {/each}\n  {/each}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Generation Functions\n\nFactory functions for one-shot generation tasks (images, speech, transcription, summarization, video). All share the same pattern: provide a `connection` or `fetcher`, call `generate()`, and read reactive state.\n\n### `createGeneration(options)`\n\nBase factory for custom generation types. All specialized functions below are built on this.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createGeneration, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-svelte\";\n\nconst gen = createGeneration({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/generate/custom\"),\n});\n\n// gen.generate({ prompt: 'Hello' })\n// gen.result, gen.isLoading, gen.error, gen.status\n```\n\n**Options:** `connection?`, `fetcher?`, `threadId?`, `body?`, `onResult?`, `onError?`, `onProgress?`, `onChunk?`\n\n**Returns:** `generate`, `result`, `isLoading`, `error`, `status`, `stop`, `reset`, `runId`, `updateBody` -- all state properties are reactive getters.\n\n### `createGenerateImage(options)`\n\nImage generation factory. `generate()` accepts `ImageGenerateInput`, result is `ImageGenerationResult`.\n\n### `createGenerateSpeech(options)`\n\nText-to-speech factory. `generate()` accepts `SpeechGenerateInput`, result is `TTSResult`.\n\n### `createTranscription(options)`\n\nAudio transcription factory. `generate()` accepts `TranscriptionGenerateInput`, result is `TranscriptionResult`.\n\n### `createSummarize(options)`\n\nText summarization factory. `generate()` accepts `SummarizeGenerateInput`, result is `SummarizationResult`.\n\n### `createGenerateVideo(options)`\n\nVideo generation factory with job polling. Returns additional `jobId` and `videoStatus` reactive getters. Accepts extra `onJobCreated?` and `onStatusUpdate?` callbacks.\n\nNo generation function includes automatic cleanup. Call `.stop()` manually when done.\n\n## `createChatClientOptions(options)`\n\nHelper to create typed chat options (re-exported from `@tanstack/ai-client`).\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { tool1, tool2 } from \"./tools\";\n\n// Create typed tools array (no 'as const' needed!)\nconst tools = [tool1, tool2];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\ntype Messages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n```\n\n## Types\n\nRe-exported from `@tanstack/ai-client`:\n\n- `UIMessage<TTools>` - Message type with tool type parameter\n- `MessagePart<TTools>` - Message part with tool type parameter\n- `TextPart` - Text content part\n- `ThinkingPart` - Thinking content part\n- `ToolCallPart<TTools>` - Tool call part (discriminated union)\n- `ToolResultPart` - Tool result part\n- `ChatClientOptions<TTools, TContext>` - Chat client options with typed client runtime context\n- `ConnectionAdapter` - Connection adapter interface\n- `InferChatMessages<T>` - Extract message type from options\n- `ChatRequestBody` - Request body type\n- `GenerationClientState` - Generation lifecycle state\n- `ImageGenerateInput` - Image generation input type\n- `SpeechGenerateInput` - Speech generation input type\n- `TranscriptionGenerateInput` - Transcription input type\n- `SummarizeGenerateInput` - Summarization input type\n- `VideoGenerateInput` - Video generation input type\n- `VideoGenerateResult` - Video generation result type\n- `VideoStatusInfo` - Video job status info\n\nRe-exported from `@tanstack/ai`:\n\n- `toolDefinition()` - Create isomorphic tool definition\n- `ToolDefinitionInstance` - Tool definition type\n- `ClientTool` - Client tool type\n- `ServerTool` - Server tool type\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n- [Client Tools](../tools/client-tools) - Learn about client-side tools\n"}
